<title>CHINA: China to ban smoking on all public transport.</title>
<headline>China to ban smoking on all public transport.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China, which has the highest number of smokers on earth, will ban lighting up on public transport from May 1, the China Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Offenders will be fined 10-50 yuan ($1.20-$6), the National Committee for Patriotic Health Campaigns said in an announcement.</p>
<p>Travellers will not be allowed to smoke in railway carriages, on planes, in ship cabins, buses, subways, taxis or in ticket halls or waiting rooms.</p>
<p>About 300 million of China's 1.2 billion people are smokers.</p>
</text>
